          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "متحفظ — mutaḥaffiẓ — \"reserved\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زوج خالتي رجل متحفظ ولا يتكلم كثيرا. zawj khālatī rajul mutaḥaffiẓ wa-lā yatakallamu kathīran. My aunt's husband is a reserved man and does not talk much."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "متحفظ (mutaḥaffiẓ) is built on the native Arabic root ḥ-f-ẓ, \"to keep, to guard\" (Lane). Ḥafiẓa, to keep, which you know, is from the same root; mutaḥaffiẓ is one who keeps himself to himself."
            }
          ]
        },
