          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فضولي — fuḍūlī — \"nosy, curious\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سأل الجار الفضولي عن راتبي. saʾala al-jār al-fuḍūlī ʿan rātibī. The nosy neighbour asked about my salary."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It can be mild (curious) or rude (nosy); the noun فضول is curiosity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فضولي (fuḍūlī) is built on the native Arabic root f-ḍ-l, \"to be over, to be in excess\" (Lane). Fuḍūl first meant what is more than enough; fuḍūlī is one who busies himself with what is not his."
            }
          ]
        },
